Verdict
==============================================================================
  - Lossless at every batch size: True.
  - Batched verification saved verify passes in 5/5 multi-sequence configurations (a batch of one has nothing to batch).
  - Peak sequences verified per target pass: 8.0. A per-sequence verifier would have needed that many passes per round, so this is the factor by which speculation and batching compose rather than conflict.
  - Wall-clock speedup on this CPU: 0.32x-1.57x.
  - Values below 1.0 are not a defect of the composition. The draft runs K passes serially per sequence per round, and this model pair (Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct against itself) is too close in cost for that to pay.
  - The plan's 2-3x claim is a GPU claim about a pair with a real cost gap, so it is neither confirmed nor refuted here. Re-run with --device cuda to measure it on a GPU.

